course: dictionary
lesson: 6570
title: Night, and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which meaning is meant. «Mercury's daytime surface reaches about 430 degrees Celsius, but at night it falls to about minus 180.» Here night means the dark time when the sun cannot be seen. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A time of darkness, not a party.
explain: Look at the words next to it. «A night at the cinema» uses night for an evening spent at an event, because the word cinema tells you what kind of night it is. «Good night» is what you say when going to sleep, so night is part of a goodbye, not a time of day.
explain: Context can also help with phrases. «A shift is a set time at work, such as a day shift or a night shift.» Night shift means work done during the dark hours. When you are unsure, swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Night is the dark time between evening and morning, when the sun cannot be seen.
fact: The Earth spins, so the side facing away from the Sun is in darkness: that is night.
fact: «Night» can also mean the evening as an event, such as «a night at the cinema».
fact: «Good night» is said when going to sleep.
fact: Nocturnal animals, like owls, are awake at night, and children need about ten hours of sleep each night.
exercise: «Mercury's daytime surface reaches about 430 degrees Celsius, but at night it falls to about minus 180.» In this sentence, what does night mean? | A type of owl | A school play at the theatre | *The dark time when the sun cannot be seen | A phrase said when going to bed
exercise: Ella reads «Good night, Grandma, see you tomorrow.» What does night mean in good night? | A dark time of the day | *A goodbye said when going to sleep | A kind of shift at work | An evening event
exercise: «We went to a night at the cinema on Friday.» What does night mean here? | A time to sleep | A cold, dark place | The dark hours of the day | *An evening spent at an event
test: «A shift is a set time at work, such as a night shift.» What does night mean in night shift? | A goodnight kiss | *Work done during the dark hours | A time of day with the sun shining | An evening at the cinema
test: «Huge numbers of animals swim up from the deep at night to feed near the surface and go back down at dawn.» What does dawn tell you about the night? | The evening is starting | *It ends when morning light appears | It means the same as day | It is the name of a fish
exam: «It was a dark and stormy night» is a cliché, a phrase used so often that it has lost its power; what does night mean here? | *The dark time between evening and morning | A phrase said when going to sleep | A type of work shift | An evening event
